# Custom UI for new features

When adding or changing product UX in `apps/rinse-mobile/`:

- **Always** use existing design-system surfaces (`AppSheet`, `Card`, list rows, pills, tokens) — not `window.prompt`, `window.confirm`, or numbered browser dialogs.
- Prefer a dedicated sheet/component (e.g. action list in `AppSheet` with `presentation="modal"`) over `Alert.alert` / `ActionSheetIOS` for multi-option product choices operators will see often.
- Native `Alert` / `ActionSheetIOS` are acceptable only for rare destructive confirms (sign out, delete) where a system dialog is already the pattern — still avoid them on web when a custom sheet exists.
- Match operator light tokens (`colors.*`, `spacing`, `radii`) and existing sheet motion; do not invent one-off chrome.

If a helper currently falls back to `prompt`/`confirm` for web, replace that path with custom UI when the flow is user-facing product UI.
